{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Noise as Ignorance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Noise as Ignorance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"noise as ignorance noise as ignorance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Noise as Ignorance.md","fileName":"Noise as Ignorance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Noise as Ignorance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Probability Interpretation and Uncertainty]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Probability Interpretation and Uncertainty","bayesianprogramming.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Noise as Ignorance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Noise as Ignorance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"noise as ignorance noise as ignorance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Noise as Ignorance.md","fileName":"Noise as Ignorance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Noise as Ignorance","heading":"Noise as Ignorance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Noise can be understood as the effect of influences that a model ignores rather than as a mysterious substance added to the phenomenon. A die throw, for example, depends on many forces and conditions that are excluded from a practical predictive model.\n\nWhat counts as signal or noise therefore depends on the description and question. Improving the available knowledge can move a formerly ignored influence into the model, changing both the predicted distribution and what remains unexplained.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Probability Interpretation and Uncertainty","bayesianprogramming.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Noise as Ignorance.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Noise as Ignorance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"noise as ignorance n